The Spanish phonemiser of sdk/audio/g2p-es.js writes the symbols eSpeak NG gives for
Spanish, mapped as misaki maps them for Kokoro; it is written from those rules and
contains no code or data of eSpeak NG. sdk/audio/g2p-en.js follows the lexicon rules
of misaki (https://github.com/hexgrad/misaki), Apache License 2.0, by hexgrad;
sdk/audio/sampler.js follows the sampler and schedule of Stability AI's
stable-audio-3 pipeline (https://github.com/Stability-AI/stable-audio-3). No code of
either is copied.

Model weights are not part of this repository. The apps download them from Hugging
Face at a pinned revision: from their original repositories, or, for SANA-Sprint
0.6B (image), from a conversion to ONNX published by UtopiaIA
(UtopiaIA/sana-sprint-0.6b-1024px-onnx-web, Apache-2.0, with its own NOTICE). Its
text encoder is Gemma 2 2B IT, provided under and subject to the Gemma Terms of Use
(ai.google.dev/gemma/terms). Their licences are listed in registry/tasks.json and
on each page. scripts/text-to-image/ holds the scripts that made that conversion.

sdk/audio/moss.js and sdk/audio/speech-moss.impl.js run MOSS-TTS-Nano (OpenMOSS,
Apache License 2.0) as its official ONNX runtime does (onnx_tts_runtime.py and
ort_cpu_runtime.py of https://github.com/OpenMOSS/MOSS-TTS-Nano); they are written
from what that runtime does, and no code of it is copied. sdk/audio/moss-voice-es.js
holds the voice prompt of Elffuss's Spanish voice: the codes MOSS-Audio-Tokenizer-Nano
gives for a recording made with Qwen3-TTS 1.7B VoiceDesign (Qwen, Apache License 2.0)
from a written description of a voice. It is a synthetic voice and not the voice of
any person. scripts/audio/moss_fixtures.py makes it and the test references.

